t's bringing people together it's  implementing good policies and it's  capably running an administration all of  those have been missing right now in  Washington and I think you know American  mayors in cities of any size I think  represent one of the levels maybe the  only level of American government left  that's generally working well well we  all like to say that all politics are  local but the last time that a sitting  mayor was nominated for president to a  major party was 1812 yeah why should you  be different why may you be the outlier  that's doing better than the last time a  reality TV star  elected president right things are  changing tectonic Li in our country and  we can't just keep doing what we've been  doing we can't nibble around the edges  of a system that no longer works the  experience of the industrial Midwest is  exactly the kind of experience that  politics forgive me but here on the  coasts has been ignoring and especially  in my party that's coming a terrible  cost let's talk about something that  you're familiar with and obviously  that's time serving overseas in  Afghanistan you spent seven months there  what do you think of the president's  potential plan now of moving troops back  home well they come home now  we've got to get out of Afghanistan I  mean there are people who are now old  enough almost to be deployed who weren't  even born when 9/11 took place we've  also got to make sure that the way we do  it doesn't leave us vulnerable as some  Intel assessments have said we would be  to being attacked again within two years  if we allow terrorist networks to  develop in a failed state it's a good  sign that the Taliban is willing to talk  and if they're serious about putting  their weapons aside that could be a  pathway to peace but I'm a little  puzzled that we haven't had the Afghan  government itself that we recognize as  legitimate government at the table we've  got to make sure that they're involved  because any piece we come up with could  very quickly collapse if we don't have  them as a party those peace talks have  not included that it's shuttle diplomacy  right they go buddy they sit down with  the Taliban in Doha then you know we're  told that Khalil Asaad was was  conferring with the Afghan government  giving them I guess the heads up but  we've got to find a way to get them to  the table when you talk about nibbling  around the edges if you look at the  other Democrats who are running they're  not nibbling around the edges they're  talking about medicare-for-all some are  talking about getting rid of private  insurance so that's the coup that's the  competition you have so what is your  idea that it is so big that it that is  nobody would mistake it for nibbling  around the edges well first of all we've  got to repair our democracy the  Electoral College needs to go because  it's made our society less and less  democratic and we can talk about a lot  of different policy ideas and we'll on  everything from security to health care  but you know our party has this tendency  to lead with the policies go to the  14-point plan and give you the binders  and the powerpoints first we got to  explain our values and explain why  Democrats are committed to freedom to  democracy to security and that democracy  peace has to  be fixed before anything else will go  well in this country just to just  clarify what what John was asking about  do you support Medicare for all I do I  also think that on the road to get there  there are a lot of other things that are  not being talked about enough  Mayor Bloomberg who was likely join the  race says it would bankrupt this country  well it would bankrupt this country if  we didn't pay for it and right now in  Washington a lot of things are being  done that aren't paid for by the way my  generation is the one that's going to  face the bill for that so as somebody  who's god-willing planning to be here in  2050 for when I reach the current age of  the curren